# PR Draft: fix(notifications): ensure processing notifications dismiss on completion or task removal (#476)

Closes #476

### Summary
Fixes an issue where the 'Processing document...' ongoing notification stayed stranded in the Android notification tray indefinitely after uploading documents.

### Root Cause & Fix
1. In PaperlessTasksApiImpl.listenForTaskChanges, querying with TaskFilterOptions(taskName: TaskNameEnum.consumeFile) and using firstWhere caused runtime exceptions on modern Paperless instances (where task names/types changed), crashing the stream and tearing down the pending task listener prematurely.
2. EventListenerShell did not detect when tasks were completed or removed from PendingTasksNotifier, leaving the ongoing notification active in the Android system shade.
3. Added cancelTaskNotification in LocalNotificationService and hooked it into EventListenerShell to cancel progress notifications whenever tasks finish or are removed.
4. Added autoCancel: true to task notification details so tapping them dismisses them.

### Verification
- Unit tests added in task_notification_lifecycle_test.dart.
- Verified on physical Android 17 device (Pixel 11 Pro).
